# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/002_conditional_compilation.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_conditional_compilation
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Nested conditional groups, defined in both spellings, arithmetic in a controlling expression, an undefined identifier evaluating to zero, and a skipped group containing text that would not survive translation
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- No signed overflow. Every value the preprocessor computes is a small integer constant
  of magnitude at most 42, and every value computed at run time is 0 or 1.
- The single shift, 1 << 4, shifts a positive int by 4, strictly within range for the
  32-bit int all four targets provide.
- No pointer, array or aggregate exists in the program, so there is no aliasing
  violation, no out-of-bounds access and no one-past-end pointer.
- No uninitialised read: dead_marker is initialised at its declaration and read
  afterwards, and it is the only object in the program.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points, and no argument of any call has a
  side effect, so nothing depends on unspecified evaluation order.
- Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the addresses of unrelated objects.
- -7 / 2 and 17 % 5 rely on truncation toward zero and a dividend-signed remainder,
  which the standard mandates from C99 onward and which were measured identical on all
  four targets, so no target restriction is needed and all three oracles stay enabled.
- The strongest observable in the program asserts an ABSENCE: a skipped group containing
  a nested true group must leave dead_marker at 0. A preprocessor that failed to skip
  the outer group would leave it at 1 or 2, which is precisely the shape of defect a
  structural token-stream test is weakest at detecting and an output oracle is strongest
  at.
- No directive appears inside a function-call argument list; every conditional is
  resolved at file scope into a plain integer macro, so every call is a single
  well-formed expression.

Verified empirically on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and qemu-user 10.1.0: the default
strict warning gate (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror) produces zero diagnostics at -O0, -O1 and -O2; the sanitizer gate
(-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all) runs to completion with no
output and exit status 0; and all twelve cells of the declared matrix produce
byte-identical stdout with exit status 0 and an empty standard error.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Every construct exercised here is documented as supported - docs/technical-specifications.md
lines 93, 94 and 493 name #ifdef, #ifndef, #if, #elif, #else and #endif evaluation and the
preprocessor constant-expression evaluator with integer arithmetic and defined(), and
docs/project-guide.md line 79 lists the same - so this program carries no
expected-divergence marker and a divergence under any oracle is a genuine finding.

The measured target differences are handled by construction, so this program needs no
target restriction and no marker:

1. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
   (docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462). No long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t
   and no pointer value is printed anywhere, and no length modifier for any of them is
   used, so the difference cannot reach the output.
2. Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured signed on x86_64 and
   i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. No plain char value is printed.
3. long double has three representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
   16 bytes, x87 80-bit against IEEE binary128). No long double appears in this program;
   that type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, which is
   the only program permitted to narrow a comparison on its account.
4. All four targets are little-endian, and no byte-order-sensitive value is printed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
nested_result=7
feature_a_on=1
feature_b_on=0
pp_arith_ok=1
undef_is_zero=1
width_in_range=1
dead_block_skipped=1
END
